    <id>https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/11/03/2026-22396/pipeline-safety-amendments-to-liquefied-natural-gas-facilities#2026-11-03</id>
    <title>Proposed rule: Pipeline Safety: Amendments to Liquefied Natural Gas Facilities</title>
    <link href="https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/11/03/2026-22396/pipeline-safety-amendments-to-liquefied-natural-gas-facilities"/>
    <updated>2026-11-03T00:00:00Z</updated>
    <summary>Notice of proposed rulemaking (NPRM). PHMSA proposes updating its regulations for liquefied natural gas (LNG) facilities to incorporate by reference the most recent industry safety standards and to make other changes to account for more than two decades of improvements and technological advancements. This rulemaking also responds to congressional mandates directing PHMSA to integrate risk-based regulatory approaches for certain LNG facilities. Affects 49 CFR 191, 49 CFR 193. Comments close 2027-01-04.</summary>
  </entry>
