  <entry>
    <id>https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/10/27/2026-21922/hazardous-materials-harmonization-with-international-standards#2026-10-27</id>
    <title>Proposed rule: Hazardous Materials: Harmonization With International Standards</title>
    <link href="https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/10/27/2026-21922/hazardous-materials-harmonization-with-international-standards"/>
    <updated>2026-10-27T00:00:00Z</updated>
    <summary>Notice of proposed rulemaking (NPRM). PHMSA proposes to update the Hazardous Materials Regulations to adopt certain international regulations and standards related to proper shipping names, hazard classes, packing groups, special provisions, packaging authorizations, air transport quantity limitations, and vessel stowage requirements. These proposed amendments are intended to maintain consistency with the latest international regulations and standards, to reduce costs to entities or individuals within the United States, and to lower the cost of regulations on the U.S. economy. Affects 49 CFR 171, 49 CFR 172, 49 CFR 173, 49 CFR 175, 49 CFR 176, 49 CFR 178, 49 CFR 180. Comments close 2026-12-28.</summary>
  </entry>
