    <id>https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/08/07/2026-16111/hazardous-materials-allowing-fireworks-certification-agencies-fcas-to-approve-professional-fireworks#2026-08-07</id>
    <title>Final rule: Hazardous Materials: Allowing Fireworks Certification Agencies (FCAs) To Approve Professional Fireworks</title>
    <link href="https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/08/07/2026-16111/hazardous-materials-allowing-fireworks-certification-agencies-fcas-to-approve-professional-fireworks"/>
    <updated>2026-08-07T00:00:00Z</updated>
    <summary>Final rule. This final rule expands the authority of a Fireworks Certification Agency (FCA) to obtain the ability to approve fireworks constructed to certain requirements. These amendments will streamline PHMSA&apos;s fireworks approval process and provide the industry with improved regulatory flexibility. Affects 49 CFR 107, 49 CFR 171, 49 CFR 172, 49 CFR 173.  Effective 2026-09-08.</summary>
  </entry>
